= {!<span class="term term-nationalist-social-democratic">!}Khalil Maleki{!</span>!}

{!<span class="term term-nationalist-social-democratic">!}Maleki{!</span>!}
advises on social-democratic organization and internal political education.
The consultation becomes available when the opposition has formed a common
coalition and does not project his later
{!<span class="term term-social-democratic">!}Third Force{!</span>!}
position backward.

- @maleki_organizers
- @maleki_program
- @main: Return to the monthly briefing

@maleki_organizers
title: Train organizers
subtitle: Organizers learn to connect social demands to the coalition without dissolving into it
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0 and front_formed = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if front_formed = 0: Available after the common electoral protest. ?][? if front_formed = 1: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before another adviser action. ?]
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; toilers_organization += 5; organizational_reach += 2

{!<span class="term term-nationalist-social-democratic">!}Maleki{!</span>!} turns a political discussion into practical organizer training:
running a small meeting, recording disagreements, recruiting follow-up
contacts, and reporting what actually happened.

The {!<span class="term term-social-democratic">!}Toilers' Party{!</span>!}
current gains people who can reproduce the work, and some of
those methods travel into the wider coalition. Other components retain their
own organizing traditions.

- @main: Return to the monthly briefing

@maleki_program
title: Clarify the social program
subtitle: <span class="term term-nationalist-social-democratic">Maleki</span> makes room for a social argument inside a coalition held together by constitutional and national demands
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0 and front_formed = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if front_formed = 0: Available after the common electoral protest. ?][? if front_formed = 1: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before another adviser action. ?]
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; toilers_relation += 4; toilers_dissent -= 3; public_mandate += 2

{!<span class="term term-nationalist-social-democratic">!}Maleki{!</span>!}
asks {!<span class="term term-social-democratic">!}Toilers' Party{!</span>!}
organizers to distinguish the social commitments they
will continue to argue for from the narrower program they can pursue through
the {!<span class="term term-national-front">!}Front{!</span>!} now. The
exercise does not erase disagreement; it makes the terms of
cooperation explicit.

Internal frustration eases, and the coalition can address social concerns
without claiming a program its other components have not accepted.

- @main: Return to the monthly briefing
